A sustained Buddhist textual investigation (@buddhist-research-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhism, #philosophy @buddhist-research-completion, #buddhism @buddhist-research-completion) { r_5KS9ZFFK5HYPAMBYJQ9ACHF3NJ
The [shared argument-reading method](../../../ancient-greek-philosophy/foundations/Read-an-argument.lingua#r_4GMQCKPBF9BCSKDK0KPN013EBN) can support the reconstruction of a Buddhist passage; use the languages and contexts the passage itself needs.

Frame a precise question that the selected corpus can answer. Read the complete relevant discourses, chapters, or treatises, and explain their argument sequence. State which language and textual decisions your claim depends on. Use [textual study](Textual-study.lingua#r_5ATB59ZTXZHDEKYE94B3ZR5H74) where wording is decisive and [careful comparison](Comparing-traditions.lingua#r_3KS8KCQ806EAZBGBRQ3H51RPY1) when crossing traditions.

Locate scholarship addressing the actual issue. Record the search terms, languages, date, editions, and references followed; seek a substantial competing account and verify it in the work attributed to its author. Distinguish a tradition’s commentary from a modern historical or philosophical reconstruction. An accessible book alone does not establish the current scholarly debate.

Develop a defensible thesis with primary passages, reconstruction of a serious alternative, objections, and replies. A contribution can clarify an ambiguity, challenge an inference, or defend a consequential interpretation. Explain how it differs from the literature you examined, and bound any claim to originality accordingly.

Present the work to an informed critic, respond to the strongest objections, and revise it. Retain the revised argument and unresolved questions. Depth rests in the textual control and reasoning demonstrated; neither a book count nor a declaration of attainment supplies them.

**Continue:** [Buddhism: a defended scholarly study](Research-completion.lingua#r_7QF5XWQYY7K78XPCQMM068YYE9).

**Return:** [Buddhism: from the path to sustained inquiry](../Buddhism.lingua#r_7P61Z6HHZNZZ8ND3DHXSFSNRRE).
